    "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:48:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-15T10:48:23Z",
    "body": "One nuance for that follow-up: at the end of the epoch after the bid, a payment that met quorum moves to `builder_pending_withdrawals`. The balance is only debited once a payload processes that withdrawal, so with a run of empty payloads (or a full withdrawal queue) the debit can land after the 3 epoch release. The fallout is limited to rejected bids, since `can_builder_cover_bid` subtracts the pending amounts. Reconciling against both pending payments and pending withdrawals, the same as `get_pending_balance_to_withdraw_for_builder`, would remove the timer entirely.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
