    "created_at": "2026-10-16T14:24:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-16T14:24:19Z",
    "body": "Thanks Marko, appreciate you tightening the retries. I checked the new adapter and noticed the BN also sets `engine.state` to `SYNCING` after an `INVALID` response, so the catch can still turn that into a retry. Could we check the result of that specific request instead? #10234 already keeps those responses separate.\n\nOn settlement, the delayed-withdrawal test in #10351 is the case I meant. Queueing a payment doesn't debit the balance, so it can remain payable beyond three epochs. I agree that keeping an already-paid bid reserved forever is wrong too. I'm continuing LOD-112 to distinguish those cases using both pending queues. Could we keep that limitation explicit until it's wired in?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
