    "created_at": "2026-10-16T14:49:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-16T14:49:46Z",
    "body": "Confirmed at f6069d7c041. `notifyForkchoiceUpdate` updates the state from the response status before it throws ([http.ts#L355](https://github.com/ChainSafe/lodestar/blob/f6069d7c041f4d66cafd0a3f0831555fff7e2be2/packages/beacon-node/src/execution/engine/http.ts#L355)), and `getExecutionEngineStateForPayloadStatus` maps `INVALID`, `INVALID_BLOCK_HASH` and `ELERROR` to `SYNCING` ([utils.ts#L171-L175](https://github.com/ChainSafe/lodestar/blob/f6069d7c041f4d66cafd0a3f0831555fff7e2be2/packages/beacon-node/src/execution/engine/utils.ts#L171-L175)). So an `INVALID` fcU passes the check at [handler.ts#L119](https://github.com/ChainSafe/lodestar/blob/f6069d7c041f4d66cafd0a3f0831555fff7e2be2/packages/cli/src/cmds/builder/handler.ts#L119) and gets retried until the deadline.\n\nJSON-RPC error responses do the same thing. The client `ERROR` event maps `ErrorJsonRpcResponse` and `HttpRpcError` to `SYNCING` ([utils.ts#L200-L207](https://github.com/ChainSafe/lodestar/blob/f6069d7c041f4d66cafd0a3f0831555fff7e2be2/packages/beacon-node/src/execution/engine/utils.ts#L200-L207)), so a permanent `-38003 Invalid payload attributes` would be retried as well. Only the `SYNCING` status branch throws `Execution Layer Syncing`, so checking the response itself like #10234 does is the reliable way.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
